    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0444" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.51/3816: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dodd</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-24T18:00:00-05:00">January 24, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Your No. 13, January 23. Referring to Schacht’s statement “that American
                    creditors and bankers did not seem to understand <pb facs="0445" n="345"
                        xml:id="pg345"/> the delicacies of Germany’s financial situation and that
                    they had no authoritative committee to negotiate any of the matters involved”,
                    unless you already did so, in your talk with Sehacht, it is highly advisable
                    that the German authorities be made to understand that the Bondholders
                    Protective Council is a disinterested body of most carefully selected
                    individuals which was brought into existence upon the initiative of this
                    Government and that the general anticipation exists that this body will play the
                    same role as the Council of Foreign Bondholders in Great Britain, and that this
                    Government has trust in it and regards it for practical purposes as representing
                    the American holders of German bonds. Mr. Laird Bell is its representative and
                    we assume that you are cooperating with him (Department’s instruction No.
                        5<anchor n="43" xml:id="d281-f1"/>).</p>
                <p>In regard to Schacht’s statement that only exchange surpluses in small amounts
                    could be used for repurchasing bonds on the market at low rates the Department
                    still awaits report as to quantities actually made available in past 2 years
                    which it requested you to ask the German Government to provide.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
